  "title": "Shipping custom models at scale from fine-tuning to inference",
  "description": "Fine tuning, serving, and inference are core components of real world AI adoption. In this panel Rob Ferguson, Daniel Han (Unsloth), Mark Saroufim (Stealth Startup) and other practitioners discuss how teams are customizing models, taking them to production, and running them efficiently at scale. The conversation covers tradeoffs in fine tuning techniques, infrastructure choices for serving, optimizing inference cost and latency, and what’s working today for builders shipping AI powered products.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
